PySpectrum is a Python package for representing and analyzing spectra using the xarray framework.

The package provides robust implementations of Spectrum and Peak objects, which include methods for:

Peak finding and center detection

Spectrum fitting and integration

Domain analysis and manipulation

Other common spectral analysis tasks

The repository also includes example notebooks demonstrating common workflows and how to use the package effectively.

PySpectrum is designed to simplify spectrum handling while providing flexibility for advanced analysis workflows.
